WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:55.220
<b>You're Fired</b>

3
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.680
Hey wait! I think I know that guy with the
sword!

4
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.140
Yeah! He's one of Straw Hat Luffy's Henchmen.
Pirate Hunter Zoro!

5
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.690
Henchman, huh?

6
00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.190
Least he recognized me. You're not even a
henchman.

7
00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.520
You're Pirate A.

8
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.070
What was that?

9
00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.360
Maybe "B"?

10
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.720
Listen, when I get a bounty,
it's gonna be twice as much as yours.

11
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.950
Whatever, Pirate C.

12
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.090
Stop changing it!

13
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.000
Hey, stop you two.

14
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.980
I don't think they can
hear you, Sniper King.

15
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.680
Don't worry.

16
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.450
It's all part of my plan.

17
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.450
I don't get it, but it sounds cool.

18
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.570
There's more of them over there!

19
00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.970
They found us!

20
00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.510
Some might be hiding on the train!

21
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.380
Blow it up!

22
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.610
Hey! Stop! Nami's still inside there!

23
00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.610
Fire!

24
00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.390
That hurt!

25
00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:47.460
Huh?

26
00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.960
Are you okay, Sniper King?

27
00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.800
Never better, my friend.

28
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.500
Whoa!

29
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.800
Cease fire!

30
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.460
What's wrong?

31
00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.460
See for yourself!

32
00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.000
Hi!

33
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.100
Don't shoot!

34
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.770
I'm just an old lady!

35
00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.770
I'm a little girl with a kitty cat!

36
00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.500
We're too cute to die!

37
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.360
Meow! Meow!

38
00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.000
The Straw Hat Pirates threatened
to do all kinds of rude

39
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.990
and immoral stuff if I didn't
operate the train for them!

40
00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.420
Those meanies!

41
00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.360
Meow! Meow!

42
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.770
Who would let their hostages get drunk?

43
00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.700
That was close!

44
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.810
We almost blew up
that innocent old lady!

45
00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.610
What kind of deranged
monster would take

46
00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:32.410
a senior citizen, a little girl,
and a cat as hostages?

47
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.230
Is it just me, or is that
smoke forming a cloud?

48
00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.300
Using cool balls.

49
00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.140
And heat balls.

50
00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.340
I can turn the moisture
in the air into clouds.

51
00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.270
Aww, there you are Nami-sweet!

52
00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.440
I knew you'd make it out okay!

53
00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.820
He didn't name it the "Perfect
Clima Takt" for nothing!

54
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.760
These clouds are growing a lot
bigger and faster than before!

55
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.530
The question is, how
strong are the thunderbolts?

56
00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.530
Let's find out.

57
00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.670
This is looking scary, guys.

58
00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.200
It's prob'ly better to run, right?

59
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.600
I hope you're ready.

60
00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.140
'Cause here comes the
new Thunderbolt Tempo!

61
00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.200
You trying to kill me or what?

62
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.870
Ah!

63
00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.910
Nami, why'd you hit Sniper King?

64
00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.840
I don't know.

65
00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:38.940
I felt like it?

66
00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.340
Don't take it out on me!

67
00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.950
It's not my fault you
don't know how to use it yet!

68
00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.510
Besides, Usopp told me he
never added a feature like that!

69
00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.190
Either way.

70
00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.640
That thing is crazy powerful!

71
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.760
You beat everyone!

72
00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.120
Ah.

73
00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:57.820
Damn it, Nami!

74
00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:58.520
What the hell?

75
00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.250
Watch where you aim that thing!

76
00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.150
Apologize to him, Sniper King!

77
00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.160
You apologize, stupid!

78
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.560
I haven't felt a shock like that since
the first time I met you, Nami-swan.

79
00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.730
Those pirates are out of control.

80
00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.700
It's crazy!

81
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.600
I thought that girl
was just the navigator,

82
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.300
but it turns out she's as
strong as the rest of 'em!

83
00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.380
So anyway, what about our Captain?

84
00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.280
Any guesses on where he went?

85
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.120
Who knows.

86
00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.490
The island's pretty big.

87
00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.620
Where should we start?

88
00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.530
Huh?

89
00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.840
That's got to be where he's at.

90
00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.620
All right, then.

91
00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.620
Let's get moving.

92
00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.300
You filthy criminals think the
Watchdogs'll let you do as you please?

93
00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.970
Not a chance!

94
00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.540
<b>Main Island, Enies Lobby</b>

95
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:10.890
Now, Gum-Gum Spear!

96
00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.090
He jumped onto the tree!

97
00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.230
I'm not getting anywhere.

98
00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.260
Don't those dumb jerks
have anything better to do?

99
00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.200
This way! Quick!

100
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.720
They're running the other way?

101
00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.180
Half of you, head to the
main island front gate!

102
00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.880
Pirates forced it open
and are invading the island!

103
00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.900
Stop them at any cost!

104
00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.840
All right, now that everyone else's here
I can finally stop running from these guys!

105
00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.210
Got him!

106
00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:42.880
Sorry!

107
00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:43.910
Try again!

108
00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.910
He's over there!

109
00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.050
Fire!

110
00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.010
<b>Main Island
At the Island Gate</b>

111
00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.390
Hey. Is something wrong?

112
00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:10.840
We are the Watchdogs, guards
of the island's front gate!

113
00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.680
You've run rampant for
far too long, villains!

114
00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.240
No criminal shall cross this line!

115
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.790
Yep, I'd say they've
got us surrounded all right.

116
00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.520
Were they following us all this time?

117
00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:35.780
Yeah?

118
00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.250
We'll see.

119
00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.310
You cocky little scoundrel!

120
00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.120
All right men, let's a...

121
00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.530
Grab on!

122
00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.790
Here!

123
00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:00.970
Thanks.

124
00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.800
Coulda let us have
some fun first, though.

125
00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.410
You idiot!

126
00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.580
Don't forget the reason you came here!

127
00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.380
Save your energy for the real fight!

128
00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.680
You're right.

129
00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.320
We'd be here all day
with that many guys.

130
00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.140
Those kiddos are full of energy!

131
00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.140
Don't die out there!

132
00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.880
Go save your friend!

133
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.880
Meow, meow!

134
00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:37.780
Everybody!

135
00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.520
Get back!

136
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.620
It's a King Bull from Water 7!

137
00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.560
Ready the cannons!

138
00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.390
You guys ready?

139
00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.660
Fire!

140
00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.690
Franky Family coming through!

141
00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.360
Watchdogs, back in
formation immediately!

142
00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.780
Roger!

143
00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.550
You can run away if you
like, but our dogs aren't going

144
00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.080
to lose to a couple of overgrown fish!

145
00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:10.780
Uh-oh!

146
00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.820
They're gonna jump up on the bull!

147
00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:13.520
What?

148
00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.020
Can't we go any faster?

149
00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.360
Hey, Cook.

150
00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.960
What's up?

151
00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.550
You take the reins.

152
00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:23.750
Here.

153
00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.060
Wait.

154
00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.810
What's going on here?

155
00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:44.270
When you see 'em, I want you
to pass on a message for me.

156
00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.240
"You're all fired."

157
00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:50.010
You got it.

158
00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.880
All right, jump!

159
00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.250
Not so fast!

160
00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.350
Good luck, Galley-La, we're
leaving this one to you!

161
00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:59.260
We're gonna skewer you!

162
00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.290
Half Knot Air Drive!

163
00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.340
Whoa!

164
00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.630
He took out those
Watchdogs out in one hit!

165
00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.330
Fools!

166
00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:15.770
They just let their guard down!

167
00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:18.280
No mere human can match our speed!

168
00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.850
Give them a taste of canine power, men!

169
00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:21.850
Go!

170
00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.840
They won't know what hit 'em!

171
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.180
Strike 'like lightning!

172
00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:34.370
Not them too!

173
00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.440
Who are these guys?

174
00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.300
That was so cool!

175
00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.420
You ready for round two?

176
00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:59.220
<b>Tower of Justice
Enies Lobby</b>

177
00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.820
Take this!

178
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:11.510
It seems your temperament is as
volatile as ever, Cutty Flam.

179
00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:14.010
Even though we haven't
seen each other in years,

180
00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.850
it turns out that you've caused
me quite a bit of trouble;

181
00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:19.910
faking your death and hiding
the blueprints, I mean.

182
00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.010
It's ironic.

183
00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:24.410
I could've arrested you had
I known you were alive.

184
00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.960
Your old charges never
were cleared were they?

185
00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.190
Speaking of thorns in my side,
your old friend Iceberg

186
00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.540
has given me quite the hassle as well.

187
00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.450
Bringing together all the ship
builders in Water 7 was quite crafty.

188
00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:42.240
The resulting Galley-La Company turned
into a force to be reckoned with.

189
00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:46.560
Though he must've resented the government,
he allied with us all the same.

190
00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.090
And before we knew it,
we were reliant on

191
00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:52.240
his company to provide
ships for the entire Navy.

192
00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.210
Not only was he the president
of the Galley-La Company.

193
00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.810
He was also the mayor of Water Seven.

194
00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.510
In other words, he was
popular with the public

195
00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.920
If we dealt with him carelessly,

196
00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.000
I've heard that your
company has been contracted

197
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.070
to build ships for the
World Government!

198
00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.020
I won't tolerate you helping them!

199
00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.660
How could you, after
what they did to Tom?

200
00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.630
So that's why he made a
deal with those bastards.

201
00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.500
I admit, he's a very clever man!

202
00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.340
Or was.

203
00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.550
I had almost lost my patience.

204
00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.710
If the wind hadn't blown
in my favor when it did,

205
00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:36.550
I was ready to resort
to extreme measures.

206
00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:39.950
Then, Admiral Aokiji sent
some good news my way.

207
00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.960
He said that our little friend
Nico Robin was on a pirate ship,

208
00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.680
headed to Water Seven for repairs.

209
00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:50.950
Of course, I had to calm down and
think about it over a cup of coffee.

210
00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.020
But fortunately, with the
Buster Call at my disposal,

211
00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:56.760
it was quite easy to formulate a plan.

212
00:12:56.760 --> 00:13:00.930
Little did I know, the result would
exceed my wildest expectations.

213
00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.170
Look!

214
00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:07.800
Both of the triggers needed to revive the
Ancient Weapon are right here at my mercy!

215
00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.830
You get it, now?

216
00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.700
When I say the winds of this
world are blowing in my favor,

217
00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.970
I most assuredly mean it!

218
00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:26.910
Every man and every nation in
the world must answer to me!

219
00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:30.380
All that power at
the tip of my fingers!

220
00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:31.910
I don't understand.

221
00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.280
Why would Aokiji allow you
to invoke the Buster Call?

222
00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.770
What gives you the
right to question me?

223
00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.740
You shut your mouth!

224
00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.340
You get to play a part in
the rebirth of this world!

225
00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:09.010
Isn't that enough for you,
you insolent witch?

226
00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:13.380
Why, you should even be thanking me!

227
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.250
Yeah? Huh?

228
00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:20.730
I'll cleanse this world of Ohara's
legacy by bleeding you dry.

229
00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:23.640
Now listen, and listen well.

230
00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:28.280
From this moment on, I'm going to make you
suffer pain so excruciatingly agonizing

231
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.480
that you'll wake up every
morning wishing you were dead.

232
00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:33.080
So prepare yourself.

233
00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:38.090
I'm going to hurt you and use you
then throw you out into the sea!

234
00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.330
A life as sinful as
yours deserves nothing less!

235
00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:50.990
Oh, and by the way, I just
received some interesting news.

236
00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.360
Apparently, a moronic
group of riff-raff has decided

237
00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:58.400
to infiltrate our island in a
hapless attempt to rescue you.

238
00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.800
You don't mean...?

239
00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:01.800
Yes.

240
00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.750
But, don't you worry.

241
00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.420
I'm sure they've been
apprehended by now.

242
00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.590
Straw Hat Luffy and his
crew will trouble us no more.

243
00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:13.610
They're so stubborn.

244
00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:17.380
They're little more
than insects compared

245
00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:21.050
to the might of the ten thousand
soldiers of Enies Lobby.

246
00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:24.890
Conveniently, we were already
preparing a prison transport ship.

247
00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.060
What perfect timing they have!

248
00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:29.450
Along with Cutty Flam, they'll
make a wonderful addition

249
00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:33.390
as the latest inmates of Impel Down.

250
00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:38.630
Hold on!

251
00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:39.630
That wasn't part of our agreement!

252
00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:41.930
In exchange for my
cooperation and surrender,

253
00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:45.700
you promised that you'd let
the Straw Hats escape safely!

254
00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.370
Come now!

255
00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:50.110
What are you getting
so worked up about?

256
00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.240
Lucci!

257
00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:54.750
Remind her of the exact
conditions that were offered!

258
00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:58.950
The terms of the arrangement were, that
excluding Nico Robin, the Straw Hat Pirates

259
00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:01.390
would be allowed to
leave Water 7 safely.

260
00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.490
Correct.

261
00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:04.090
There you have it.

262
00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:07.860
Fairly straightforward, I'd say.

263
00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.020
After allowing them
to leave Water 7 safely,

264
00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:20.190
as promised, the Straw Hats
decided to come here.

265
00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.340
Is this some kind of joke?

266
00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:28.510
You're going to break the heart of our
agreement over a ridiculous technicality?

267
00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.020
These dirtbags are
the lowest of the low.

268
00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.620
Not a shred of decency
in any one of 'em!

269
00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:34.960
Huh?

270
00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.240
What did you say?

271
00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.470
Shut up, you filthy piece of trash!

272
00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:43.760
We're not under any obligation to keep
our promises to a bunch of criminals!

273
00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.090
You hear me?

274
00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:47.730
Take that, and that, and that!

275
00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:48.760
You, too!

276
00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.430
Don't get cocky with me, understand?

277
00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:56.100
Deceiving and capturing pirates is
what the Navy does, you insolent wench!

278
00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:58.340
You're just the idiot who fell for it!

279
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.300
You coward.

280
00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.080
Still running that mouth of yours, I see.

281
00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:10.780
Rest assured.

282
00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:11.980
I'll choose a fitting death for one

283
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:16.980
who's spent her life lying,
deceiving, and betraying others.

284
00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:25.160
Before the supreme power of
justice, resistance is futile.

285
00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:30.200
But look on the bright side, at least
your friends will suffer and die with you!

286
00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:38.660
Hey!

287
00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.570
What's all that commotion about?

288
00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.510
Something's coming!

289
00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.520
Way to go, Sodom and Gomorrah!

290
00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.620
Keep charging forward!

291
00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:08.860
Oh, no!

292
00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:10.030
It's them!

293
00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.800
Those pirates that broke
through the Main Island's Gate!

294
00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.630
Fire!

295
00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.400
Don't let up!

296
00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.830
Gero, Gero! Gero, Gero!

297
00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:19.400
Unless you wanna die,
get outta the way!

298
00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:20.100
Take that!

299
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:20.970
And that!

300
00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:25.570
Fall back and then restore formation!

301
00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.280
Damn!

302
00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:28.980
Stupid pirates!

303
00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:31.250
You shouldn't be so cocky!

304
00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.700
Now I've got you, pirate lady!

305
00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:48.250
Get outta here!

306
00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.080
Beat it!

307
00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.480
Smooth sailing.

308
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.120
These two make it easy.

309
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:55.120
Keep going until we reach
our Captain, King Bulls!

310
00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:58.700
Hurry!

311
00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.100
Don't let him escape!

312
00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.170
He's alone!

313
00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:02.740
Surround him!

314
00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:05.940
Get him!

315
00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.080
Move!

316
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.850
Get outta my way!

317
00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:18.280
Stupid bastards!

318
00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:19.750
Commander!

319
00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.920
This guy's really scary!

320
00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.220
Don't falter, men!

321
00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.190
Bring him down!

322
00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:26.250
Attack!

323
00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:30.120
Commander!

324
00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.490
There! Yep!

325
00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:38.930
That dead end's gotta be the place!

326
00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:41.340
They better not
have taken you away yet!

327
00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:46.010
Robin!

328
00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.510
I suppose that's enough for now.

329
00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.210
You two!

330
00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.310
Get them out of here.

331
00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:52.420
Yes, sir!

332
00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.950
There's a Sea Prism Stone
lock on her restraints.

333
00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.330
Make sure it's secure.

334
00:19:56.330 --> 00:20:00.270
Cutty Flam goes to Impel Down and
Nico Robin to Navy Headquarters.

335
00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:04.310
As soon as the ship's ready, we'll
set sail through the Gates of Justice.

336
00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:05.210
Right!

337
00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.170
It shall be done, sir!

338
00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:10.880
Also, take extra
precautions with Cutty Flam.

339
00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:16.820
He can be extremely violen...
Has Straw Hat been sighted?

340
00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.140
Yeah.

341
00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:23.450
We got a report about it a
little while back, chapapa.

342
00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.720
When he heard the news,
Chief got so worked up.

343
00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:27.420
It was embarrassing.

344
00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:31.120
They said there were only five
casualties, but that can't be right.

345
00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.260
The receiver is off the hook.

346
00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:39.830
Don't give us any trouble, tough guy.

347
00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.000
Let's get going.

348
00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:54.890
You can return to
your quarters for now.

349
00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:58.600
Thanks to this catch, CP9 will be
the toast of Navy Headquarters.

350
00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:03.600
Our status will rise to incredible
heights, in a covert way, of course.

351
00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:07.370
And for that, I'd like to propose
a little toast of our own!

352
00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:12.380
I'm not in the mood
for some ridiculous toast.

353
00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:17.880
Nor am I interested in our
status or political influence.

354
00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:21.650
Our brand of justice is to assassinate
in the name of the World Government.

355
00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:25.420
As long as they continue to recognize
you as the commander of CP9,

356
00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:29.020
we will fulfill our duty to the letter.

357
00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:35.220
But we're under no obligation
to support your personal ideologies.

358
00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:38.360
That's... That's a sound argument.

359
00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.260
But then, what is it you want exactly?

360
00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:47.470
Perhaps all that we seek is blood.

361
00:21:56.070 --> 00:22:00.270
And with CP9, we have
the privilege to kill.

362
00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:06.290
These guys give me the creeps.

363
00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:11.000
Like he said, they assassinate
legally in the name of justice.

364
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.200
And they're very good at what they do.

365
00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:15.230
Quite dependable.

366
00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:19.310
As long as I have them working for me,
there's nothing I can't accomplish!

367
00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:20.770
I'm invincible!

368
00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:30.870
<b>Courthouse</b>
<b>Island Gate</b>

369
00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:29.360
Lieutenant Commander!

370
00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:30.630
Terrible news!

371
00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:31.330
What is it?

372
00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:31.580
<b>Courthouse</b>

373
00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:31.370
<b>Island Gate</b>

374
00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:33.940
It's Straw Hat Luffy, sir!

375
00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:38.080
We can't find him anywhere!

376
00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:39.650
He gave us the slip!

377
00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:41.220
That's impossible!

378
00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:43.650
We've got thousands of
Marines here looking for him!

379
00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:45.780
Even so, no one can find him!

380
00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:46.690
Don't tell me.

381
00:22:46.690 --> 00:22:49.230
Is he somehow already
inside the courthouse?

382
00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:50.460
No!

383
00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:53.530
Not even an insect could've
gotten past our defenses, sir!

384
00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:55.440
Go!

385
00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:58.280
We must find Straw Hat
at any cost, men!

386
00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:07.290
This is the last building.

387
00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.360
She's gotta be here.

388
00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:09.960
But there isn't a bridge.

389
00:23:09.960 --> 00:23:11.390
Looks kinda far, too.

390
00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:12.060
Oh well.

391
00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:13.530
Guess I'll try jumping over.

392
00:23:18.820 --> 00:23:19.590
What the heck?

393
00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:22.270
Air Door.

394
00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:32.700
Hey!

395
00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:34.700
You're the bull who's working
with that stupid pigeon guy!

396
00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:39.470
There seem to be some discrepancies between
the report and the actual situation.

397
00:23:39.470 --> 00:23:40.170
Whoa!

398
00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:41.810
How'd you just appear like that?

399
00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:43.140
Awesome!

400
00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:44.170
Magic?

401
00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:46.240
To be honest, it did
seem a little suspicious.

402
00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:48.750
No way you only took out 5 marines.

403
00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.950
Man, you really surprised me!

404
00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:53.420
An invasion like this is unprecedented.

405
00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:56.320
This is the furthest
anyone has ever infiltrated

406
00:23:56.320 --> 00:23:58.630
into the mouth of the World Government.

407
00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:00.300
But that ends here.

408
00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:01.050
Tell me.

409
00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:05.020
How long do you plan to keep fighting?

410
00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:19.810
Until I die.
